 "ground_glass_rebate": "The later picture resolves the far right-hand ground pane under steep obliquity, including dark pixel (465,376). At the retained camera/frames, a 35 mm recess obscures two photographed glass areas, 5 mm sends the near model’s ray into the putty, and a 4 mm recess exposes both observed panes at both detail levels. This is a camera-dependent reconstruction of a shallow glazing rebate; the original wood depth is not directly measured to millimetre precision.",
 "figure06_lower_left_sample_correction": "The first reading at (366,816) was dark glass. The original native sRGB value is [183,173,172]; two rows below it is [22,12,13]. Native pixels confirm this same point is the pale lower sash head and it is retained as such."
